# []R_ETRY e runs the body again; a counter in a ! variable shows how
# many times. The retries are limited, so a body that always fails
# ends with its error after the limit.
== SOURCE
n! := 0
u:f_laky := { @ -> n! := n! + 1; n! < 3 ? "again" []S_IGNAL "not yet"; n! }
'u:f_laky []T_RAP '{ e -> []R_ETRY e }
n!
== TYPE
n! : Int
u:f_laky : Unit -> Int
Int
Int
== RESULT
3
3
